.TH MGIT 1 "2026-07-27" "Knowledge Islands" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mgit \- run commands across multiple Git repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.TP
.B mgit
List the repositories in the current set.
.TP
.B mgit [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIcommand\fR ...]
Run
.B git
with the supplied command and arguments in every repository in the current set.
.TP
.B mgit [\fIoptions\fR] \-B \fIcommand\fR [\fIargument\fR ...]
Run a command directly, without prefixing it with
.BR git ,
in every repository in the current set.
.TP
.B mgit register
Generate
.I .mgitconfig
manifests for the current tree.
.TP
.B mgit bootstrap
Clone missing repositories declared by the current
.I .mgitconfig
manifest.
.TP
.B mgit structure \fIstandard|nested\fR \fB\-\-dry-run|\-\-yes\fR
Convert every eligible repository in the current set between standard and nested structures.
.TP
.B mgit worktree \fIlist|status\fR
List worktrees or show their branch and cleanliness.
.TP
.B mgit worktree add \fIBRANCH\fR
Add a linked checkout for an existing remote branch in every structured repository.
.TP
.B mgit worktree remove \fIPATH\fR \fB\-\-yes\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR]
Remove one linked worktree.
.TP
.B mgit completion \fIbash|zsh\fR
Print shell completion source.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mgit
runs a Git command, or an arbitrary command with
.BR \-B ,
across a set of repositories.
Before each invocation it prints the repository path and command.
With no command it prints the repository paths that would be used.
.PP
The set comes from a
.I .mgitconfig
in the current directory when one is present.
Otherwise,
.B mgit
walks the current tree for Git repositories, omitting repositories nested inside another repository.
The
.B \-I
option always uses discovery instead of manifests.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-P , " \-\-physical"
Do not follow symlinked container directories.
This is the default.
Symlinked repositories are never followed.
.TP
.BR \-L , " \-\-follow-symlinks"
Follow symlinked container directories while discovering repositories.
.TP
.BR \-B , " \-\-bare"
Run the supplied command directly rather than as a
.B git
subcommand.
.TP
.BR \-I , " \-\-ignore"
Ignore
.I .mgitconfig
files and discover repositories by walking the tree.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS register
.B mgit register
scans the current tree and writes a
.I .mgitconfig
in every container directory, listing child containers and repositories.
It also writes a manifest in a repository that owns cross-repository symlinks.
The command does not descend into repositories, always performs a fresh scan, and overwrites generated manifests.
.PP
When Chezmoi is installed and configured, generated manifests below its target directory are added to Chezmoi's source state.
.SS bootstrap
.B mgit bootstrap
uses the manifest in the current directory to clone every missing typed repository entry with a source URL.
It creates standard, nested, and bare repositories in their declared forms.
Existing paths are never replaced: a present repository must match its declared structure, and directory entries must already exist.
.SS structure
.B mgit structure nested
converts each eligible clean, attached standard checkout to a nested repository.
.B mgit structure standard
performs the reverse conversion only when the nested repository has its required
.I main/
checkout and no other linked worktrees.
.PP
Both forms require exactly one of
.B \-\-dry-run
to preview changes or
.B \-\-yes
to make them.
.SS worktree
.B mgit worktree list
groups linked worktrees by their shared Git store.
.B mgit worktree status
shows each worktree's branch and cleanliness.
.PP
.B mgit worktree add \fIBRANCH\fR
adds a checkout for an existing
.B origin/\fIBRANCH\fR
to every structured repository after preflighting the full set.
.B mgit worktree remove \fIPATH\fR \fB\-\-yes\fR
removes one linked checkout and never removes the primary or required
.I main/
checkout.
Pass
.B \-\-force
to discard dirty changes in that linked checkout.
.SS completion
.B mgit completion bash
and
.B mgit completion zsh
print shell completion definitions to standard output.
For example, source the Bash definition with:
.PP
.nf
source <(mgit completion bash)
.fi
.SH MANIFESTS
A
.I .mgitconfig
line may declare a child repository or container directory:
.PP
.nf
standard path [-> clone-url]
nested path [-> clone-url]
bare path [-> clone-url]
dir path
.fi
.PP
An untyped path remains valid for compatibility.
A line of the form
.B link -> target
declares a symlink the current repository owns and whose target is in another repository.
Blank lines and comments beginning with
.B #
are ignored.
Relative paths are resolved from the manifest's directory; absolute and
.B ~/
paths are also accepted.
.SH REPOSITORY STRUCTURES
A standard repository is an ordinary checkout with a
.I .git/
directory.
A nested repository is an
.B mgit
controller containing a
.I .bare/
shared Git store, a
.I .git
controller file, and a required
.I main/
checkout.
Commands operate in live checkouts, never in the nested controller or bare store.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .mgitconfig
Optional repository-set manifest in the current directory and nested container directories.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested operation completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An operation failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command grammar was invalid, a required confirmation was absent, or an unsupported option was supplied.
.PP
For a fan-out command,
.B mgit
returns the exit status of the last command it invokes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-worktree (1)
.PP
The project README and the worktree structures guide are available at
.I https://github.com/knowledgeislands/tools-mgit .
